  "description": "Linux Secret Service (libsecret) provider for OutWit.Shared.Secrets, for interactive desktop sessions with an unlocked keyring. The Secret Service is a session service: a systemd unit with no session, or a container, has no session bus — the honest answer there is SecretStatus.Unavailable, and the File provider is the deliberate choice. Payloads are stored base64-encoded (the libsecret password API is string-based); find entries with secret-tool lookup key {key}.",
